1
00:00:00,335 --> 00:00:02,585
Octopuses have a central brain

2
00:00:02,485 --> 00:00:03,910
but they also have a cluster

3
00:00:03,735 --> 00:00:06,285
of neurons in each of their eight arms

4
00:00:06,590 --> 00:00:09,690
Roughly 500 million neurons power them

5
00:00:09,665 --> 00:00:11,015
About two-thirds of those

6
00:00:10,865 --> 00:00:11,940
are in their limbs

7
00:00:11,840 --> 00:00:13,890
which act semi-independently

8
00:00:14,205 --> 00:00:16,555
Every sucker can taste what it touches

9
00:00:16,530 --> 00:00:18,230
This lets them solve puzzles

10
00:00:18,155 --> 00:00:19,255
open jars

11
00:00:19,155 --> 00:00:21,205
and navigate complex mazes

12
00:00:21,510 --> 00:00:23,160
In 2016

13
00:00:23,085 --> 00:00:25,360
Inky the octopus famously escaped

14
00:00:25,185 --> 00:00:26,660
a New Zealand aquarium

15
00:00:26,535 --> 00:00:29,085
by squeezing through a narrow drainpipe

16
00:00:29,365 --> 00:00:31,165
They can instantly change color

17
00:00:31,015 --> 00:00:32,790
and texture to camouflage

18
00:00:32,715 --> 00:00:34,415
yet most species live only

19
00:00:34,290 --> 00:00:35,590
1 to 2 years

20
00:00:35,890 --> 00:00:36,915
They learn alone

21
00:00:36,815 --> 00:00:38,065
without parents

22
00:00:38,015 --> 00:00:39,465
This intelligence evolved

23
00:00:39,340 --> 00:00:40,715
separately from ours

24
00:00:40,665 --> 00:00:43,040
Follow for one new idea every day
